  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nWe have fair weather with mostly clear skies this morning \nthanks to high pressure still incontrol nearby. The high\npressure system will slowly move eastwards today and a cold\nfront will approach the area from the northwest this evening.\nAhead of the cold front, southwesterly flow will increase today\n10 to 15 mph with gusts up to 25 mph during the midday and\nafternoon hours. Blue skies and lots of sunshine today will\nfavor warmer high temps this afternoon, climbing into the lower\n70s for NWPA and NEOH. Mid to upper 70s are expected this\nafternoon across north central and Northwest Ohio. A mainly dry\ncold front will move through later this evening. There could be\na couple spotty rain showers along the frontal passage over far\nNEOH and NWPA this evening, but most areas will not see any\nrainfall. A slightly cooler and breezy northwest flow will \nfollow behind the front late tonight and Thursday. Another high\npressure system will build in over the Ohio Valley for Thursday\nand Friday with high temps closer to seasonable averages for \nearly October, middle 60s to a few low 70s. Relatively quiet and\ndry weather will continue through most of Saturday before some\nchanges arrive later in the weekend. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nThe tropical system that is currently developing in the Gulf of\nAmerica and will impact the northern Gulf Coast region later \nthis week may track across the Ohio Valley later this weekend,\nbringing the potential for widespread rainfall. Forecast\nguidance and confidence is now increasing for the remnant low\npressure system will track across the Ohio Valley Saturday night\nthrough Monday with widespread showers and isolated thunder.\nAhead of the system on Saturday, high temperatures may climb\nback upwards in the mid 70s to around 80 degrees thanks to some\nsubsidence around the approaching remnant tropical system. It \nwill continue to stay warm and somewhat humid Sunday and Monday \nwith the influx of tropical moisture over the region. Despite \nrain chances likely Sunday and Monday, high temps will still \nreach the upper 60s to low 70s. It appears that a cold front \nwill arrive and move through late Monday with additional rain \nchances and cooler weather by next Tuesday and Wednesday.",
